selection: no timerfd_gettime() on QNX; restart the auto-scroll timer

QNX's timerfd (libtimerfd) implements timerfd_create() and
timerfd_settime() but not timerfd_gettime(). The selection auto-scroll reads
the timer only to keep a running timer's remaining time when the scroll
speed changes; on QNX the timer is restarted to fire at once instead (the
next scroll step comes immediately, then at the new interval).

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific

--- a/selection.c
+++ b/selection.c
@@ -1729,10 +1729,15 @@
     }
 
     struct itimerspec timer;
+#if defined(__QNX__)
+    /* no timerfd_gettime() on QNX: (re)start the timer at once */
+    memset(&timer, 0, sizeof(timer));
+#else
     if (timerfd_gettime(term->selection.auto_scroll.fd, &timer) < 0) {
         LOG_ERRNO("failed to get current selection scroll timer value");
         goto err;
     }
+#endif
 
     if (timer.it_value.tv_sec == 0 && timer.it_value.tv_nsec == 0)
         timer.it_value.tv_nsec = 1;
